# *** THREE CONSTRAINTS SHAPE THIS BLOCK. READ BEFORE EDITING. ***
#
# 1. CAREER SLUGS MUST NEVER APPEAR HERE. /about/vendors/<career-slug> serves
#    a live career page. This is subtle now: step 4 converts career vendors
#    into partnerVendors entries so their HISTORY renders from the shared
#    route - which means a generator reading partnerVendors will happily emit
#    a redirect that kills the career page. It did, for six of them, and was
#    caught by counting. The list below EXCLUDES anything that is also a
#    career slug, and must keep doing so as the remaining conversions land.
#
# 2. LIMITS: 2,000 static + 100 dynamic; rules past either are dropped
#    SILENTLY with no build error. An earlier version wrote 89 profiles x 16
#    locales = 1,424 statics and put the file at 2,056 - over. Per-slug rules
#    are now written for the two AUTHORED locales only.
#
# 3. ORDER: 'Static redirects should appear before dynamic redirects.'
#    Backwards also drops rules silently. Statics first below.
#
# And no single wildcard for all of it, because Cloudflare states that
# 'redirects are always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset
# matches the incoming request' - so a splat on /about/vendors/* would
# capture the career pages too.
# ===========================================================================

